WEBVTT

00:20:28.363 --> 00:20:31.036
when there was a heatwave,
they checked on the old people

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:32.354
and they saved their lives.

00:20:32.378 --> 00:20:34.522
In another neighborhood,
there was no library.

00:20:34.546 --> 00:20:37.615
They didn't know each other.
The old people died in the heatwave.

00:20:37.639 --> 00:20:39.631
CA: I presume it wasn't just the library.

00:20:39.655 --> 00:20:42.242
It's not like you can fix this
by putting in a library.

00:20:42.266 --> 00:20:45.570
It's that the library is a symptom
of a broader sort of interest in --

00:20:45.594 --> 00:20:48.997
DB: Social success and economic success
flow from social trust, frankly.

00:20:49.021 --> 00:20:51.888
Us guys, we want to talk
about the market and all that stuff,

00:20:51.912 --> 00:20:54.199
but there's no escaping
the realm of the intimate

00:20:54.223 --> 00:20:56.701
because if you don't have
those intimate connections,

00:20:56.725 --> 00:20:57.971
you don't have an economy.

00:20:57.995 --> 00:21:03.494
CA: But the challenge with the view that
the neighborhood is the unit of change,